<title>INDIA: India approves Kellogg proposal to increase stake.</title>
<headline>India approves Kellogg proposal to increase stake.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>India on Wednesday approved a proposal of the U.S.-based Kellogg Corp to invest $12.57 million in foreign direct investment in a fully owned subsidiary, the Industry Ministry said.  </p>
<p>The proposal is to make breakfast cereals in India.</p>
<p>Kellogg's had said earlier in March that it would launch its Frosted Flakes brand in India under the name &quot;Kellogg's Frosties.&quot;</p>
<p>Kellogg's Frosted Flakes is marketed in about 50 countries.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
